WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
Treasure Island

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.900
Silver! Behind you!

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:15.500
Silver!

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:28.250
Alright, now's our chance!
Let's rescue Jim! Charge!

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.050
Get 'em!

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.980
<i>The battle against the pirates...</i>

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:39.310
<i>...that started when we arrived on the island,</i>

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:42.080
<i>had finally reached its conclusion on Skeleton Island.</i>

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:59.400
<i>Additionally, Silver was wounded and is now our prisoner.</i>

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.940
Treasure
Island

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.740
Takarajima

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.550
saa ikou

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.550
Come, let's go

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.640
yume ni mita shima heto

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.640
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:21.480
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:21.480
Across the waves, on the wind

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:24.360
umi hedeyou

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:24.360
We'll travel the oceans

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:27.280
ikute ni wa

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:27.280
Many of us

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:30.280
minna mada shiranai

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:30.280
Still don't know of

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:34.030
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:34.030
The days and nights full of mystery

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.530
matte iru darou

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.530
That await us there

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:40.040
itsumo shinji you

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:40.040
We must always have trust

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:43.290
magokoro wo

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:43.290
And be sincere

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:49.550
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:49.550
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.680
tade hitotsu no

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.680
I only...

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:56.100
akogare dake wa

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:56.100
...have one desire

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.390
doko no dare ni mo

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.390
And no one...

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:05.100
kese wa shinai sa

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:05.100
...will ever take it away

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.650
tade hitotsu no

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.650
I only...

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.950
akogare dake wa

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.950
...have one desire

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.280
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.280
And no one...

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:24.210
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:24.210
...will ever take it away

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:41.020
episode

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:41.020
The Flying Man:
\h    Puppy the Seagull!

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:54.230
Just like that, my life is in your hands?

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:58.510
Yes, John Silver.
You are our prisoner.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:03.120
You can no longer escape.
Besides, all the others are dead.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.080
Only Puppy is left.

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:22.220
You can't kill me.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:37.020
You have a very good reason to let me live.

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:39.530
I don't see any such reason.
None exists!

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:42.530
For all your crimes,

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:44.890
you deserve the noose.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:48.660
We could also maroon you and not dirty our hands.

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:55.380
Of course, we are British gentlemen.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.540
On top of that, I'm a physician.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:02.510
We will assist you until you
can be judged on our return.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:07.350
Thank you very much.
I don't need your pity, though.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.160
Even without it,

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:12.610
it's still in your best interests to keep me alive.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.900
What's that?
You're pushing your luck!

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.190
Have you solved the riddle?

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:19.830
Wh-What did you say?

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:23.740
"A bell on a full-moon night..."

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:26.510
"The mansion of Flint."

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:30.540
"45 degrees with a spyglass on the Devil's Throne."

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:34.740
So, gentlemen?

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:37.460
Have you deciphered this strange message?

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.380
Well?

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.420
You won't solve anything without me.

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:45.150
Out of all the men in old Flint's crew,

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:48.200
I, John Silver, knew him best.

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:03.700
What?!
We'll do just fine without you!

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:07.700
Wait, Trelawney...
I hate to say it, but he's right.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:12.830
Even if we were the ones to discover the hidden paragraphs,

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:17.430
we're incapable of figuring out the meaning.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:20.130
Well, I guess that's true...

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.310
In any case, Silver is seriously wounded.

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:24.190
We can't leave him here like this.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:27.920
We'll return to the fort.
There, I can treat him.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.610
Jim, hold Silver's leg.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:48.440
Yes, sir.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.800
"A bell...

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:16.330
...o-on the full-moon night..."

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:18.750
"The mansion of Flint..."

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:22.320
"45 degrees with a spyglass...

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:25.150
...on the Devil's Throne..."

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:26.780
"Aim...

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.110
...aim the light..."

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:35.610
He's talking in his sleep.

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:37.500
Tch, you're worrying for nothing.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.920
It's almost frightening.
Silver's...

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:44.500
...incredible will.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:50.910
It's this unusual willpower that allowed Silver to win Flint's respect.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:57.560
Even if you didn't treat him, I'm sure that he would have survived.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:01.270
He'd continue to search for the treasure, even if he had to crawl.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.490
Puppy has escaped!

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:18.080
Hold it!

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.960
Let me go!

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.880
I was just doing what Silver ordered!

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:31.910
So have mercy!

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:34.180
If I go before the judge, surely I'll be hanged!

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:35.640
I don't want that!

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.600
No one said you'll be hanged for sure.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:40.980
Yeah, right!

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:43.570
Pirates always end up with a rope around their necks!

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:45.460
Please, anything but that!

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:47.190
I can't die.

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:51.450
Unlike Silver who can strike a deal by solving the riddle, I can't do anything!

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:54.870
Have mercy, let me go!

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:59.280
Come inside quickly.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:02.330
If you catch a cold, I'll have
another patient to deal with.

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:23.550
Silver!

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.880
Silver has...

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:27.810
Silver has come to!

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:31.190
Silver's opened his eyes!

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.750
What's this, Puppy?
Have you been tied up?

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.050
Poor thing.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.800
Don't think too little of this, Silver.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.510
Just like Puppy, you are our prisoner.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:02.020
There you are, Gray.
Calm down, I won't do anything.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:21.870
So, gentlemen, have you solved the riddle?

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:24.880
"A bell on a full-moon night..."

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:26.080
That must mean...

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:28.520
"The chime of a clockwork."

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:31.630
That is to say, at half past midnight.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:34.300
Yes, exactly.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:38.260
However, we don't know
what the Mansion of Flint is.

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:40.260
Can you enlighten us?

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.720
I think that the "Mansion of Flint"...

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:46.940
...signifies a particular location.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.880
As for the "Devil's Throne"...

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:52.530
I don't understand it at all.

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:57.490
It's about time for you to keep your promise.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:59.780
First, untie Puppy.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:05.450
Next, I would like to drink a hot cup of coffee.

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.760
Wh-Wha-What?!

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:11.420
Know your place, Silver.
We don't take orders from a prisoner.

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:15.880
Orders? No such thing.
I'm only asking for an exchange.

00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:18.870
Don't you also have a service to ask of me?

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:20.880
"Solve that riddle."

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.350
Isn't that right, hm?

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.180
Isn't that right, hm?

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:35.610
If you want to see your country again,
you'd better cooperate.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.880
Of course, you won't escape court.

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:42.160
However, if you ever run away,
we won't come looking for you.

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:44.540
Instead, we'll be treating you like an enemy.

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:47.320
U-Understood!

00:10:47.320 --> 00:10:48.080
Puppy!

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:49.830
Where are you going?

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:52.360
There's no one else left on this island!

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:56.070
I prefer to be on my own anyway.
Don't worry about me!

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:10.560
What is it, Silver?

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:16.150
Silver, don't move.

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:17.030
It's alright.

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:19.330
It's just aches a little, Doc...

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:20.180
Get out of the way!

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:23.490
We have no time to lose.

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:26.370
We still have one week before the full moon.

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:31.250
In the meantime, we must discover where the "Mansion of Flint" is.

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:32.880
What now, Silver?

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:36.340
Do you know where it is?

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:40.130
No, truthfully, I don't have the slightest idea.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:42.260
Wait!

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:46.680
Bastard! You said you knew the key to the riddle, yet you refuse to tell us?!

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:49.020
Hey now, I'm not refusing to tell you.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:52.220
I merely said that I was the only one who can solve this riddle.

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:55.480
I never said I had already solved it.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:00.970
Let's go, mates! Get ready to set off.
No more dawdling!

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:09.580
Let's see...

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:13.060
"A bell on a full-moon night..."

00:12:13.060 --> 00:12:14.520
"The Mansion of Flint..."

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:16.130
"The Devil's Throne..."

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:21.170
And then...
After that, let's see...

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:30.260
I've decided.
I'm a man. I'll do it!

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:32.940
I'll find the treasure and keep it for myself.

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:00.420
Silver, does it hurt?

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:03.840
No, Jim.
I'm alright.

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:06.340
Really?
I'm glad.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:09.180
You have something to say to me?

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:10.680
N-No.

00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:20.020
In the end, we've walked all day without finding a single clue.

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:24.540
No, perhaps we passed them without even noticing.

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:25.780
And if that's the case,

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:29.950
we could go around the whole island without seeing anything.

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:35.040
Are we looking for a rock or wood?
Perhaps a mark made by Flint?

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:39.880
We all have our assumptions of the location,

00:13:40.350 --> 00:13:44.370
but the treasure could be
somewhere else entirely.

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:49.580
I-If you ask me... I've lived alone
on this island for ten years,

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:52.350
but I don't understand what it means.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:57.810
And you, Silver, what is your take on it?

00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:06.900
Answer, Silver!
Do you take us for idiots?

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:10.450
I'm not taking you for idiots in particular.

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:14.580
It's just, I don't have the heart to chat.

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:17.540
I'm having trouble staying awake.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.920
He's burning with fever.

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:27.020
It's malaria.

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:32.010
His wound has weakened him and he's caught malaria.

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:38.980
What, malaria?

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:46.060
This is what I feared the most.

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:51.530
Big-Eyes, The Barrel and Anderson all died from malaria.

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:56.820
And now, it is I who has caught it.

00:14:56.820 --> 00:14:58.580
What luck...

00:14:58.580 --> 00:14:59.670
Silver...

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:01.260
Goodbye, Jim.

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:06.930
None of you move!

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:09.880
Gray, drop your gun.

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:14.270
Silver, what on earth are you doing?

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:19.370
Sorry, but I'm going.
If you follow me, I'll fire.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:25.900
Silver, where do you expect to go in that state?

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:27.190
You must be treated!

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:31.250
Don't bother hiding the truth, Doc.

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:34.820
You tried to help Anderson,
but that didn't save him.

00:15:34.820 --> 00:15:40.460
I'm strong, but malaria isn't forgiving.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:45.900
Anyhow, it's here that our roads part.

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:46.790
Goodbye!

00:15:51.460 --> 00:15:52.800
SILVER!

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:55.660
Jim, stay here!

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:56.740
Wait!

00:15:56.740 --> 00:15:57.890
Jim!

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:02.570
Me too!

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:05.150
Gray!
Ben Gunn!

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:07.070
Wait!

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:13.780
I have a feeling that something's happened.

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:16.160
Alrighty, I'll go take a look.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:38.260
This way!

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:38.680
Okay!

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:40.180
Silver!

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:46.480
Where do you expect to go
in that state, Silver?!

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:49.980
Return to the camp, Jim.
I'll fire if you don't!

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:53.200
Where are you going, Silver?

00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:56.640
Silver!

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:57.670
I'm going to fire!

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:06.540
Silver!

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:18.010
Silver!
Silver! Silver!

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:40.330
Damnit, let me go!

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:45.220
I don't have very long.

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:47.980
I must find Flint's treasure at all costs.

00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:50.880
That's my philosophy...

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.860
When I've set my mind to something,

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:54.760
no one can stop me.

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:58.500
This will be the last adventure of John Silver.

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:00.990
And I want to do it alone!

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:13.380
Wait!

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:16.740
Just wait a moment.
A few years ago...

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:20.700
I had a very high fever and I survived.

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:26.700
And I haven't had it again
ever since I recovered from it.

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:29.540
Wait a minute...
Let me see...

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:31.000
That's it!
Yes.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:33.940
There's a swamp downstream of the river.

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:36.980
You'll find some strange water lilies there.

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:39.470
I survived because I ate those flowers.

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:47.060
Are you sure about this swamp, Ben Gunn?

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:49.220
Jim!

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:50.980
Take care of Silver!

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:54.520
Jim!

00:18:57.040 --> 00:18:58.500
I'll be damned...

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:00.160
What courage!

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:10.460
Alrighty!
I'm a man, too!

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:21.390
I can't take any more...

00:19:24.310 --> 00:19:25.510
See ya!

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:28.140
Stay put and get some rest!

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:28.140
Puppy!

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:38.770
You've gotta be kiddin' me!

00:20:07.570 --> 00:20:09.950
I've found it.
There it is...

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:23.240
Why...
Why did I do this?

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:32.030
I have nine hungry brothers who are waiting back home.

00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:39.210
That's why I usually don't do anything that doesn't involve money.

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:40.800
So why...

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:43.470
Why did I do this for Silver?

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:48.970
Benbow! Benbow! Benbow!

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:50.360
Benbow! Benbow!

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:01.120
Wait, I ran away!

00:21:01.120 --> 00:21:02.780
I can't come back like this.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:05.480
<i>I'll find the treasure myself!</i>

00:21:05.480 --> 00:21:08.000
<i>Then my brothers can eat their fill!</i>

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.450
<i>We'll never be poor again!</i>

00:21:22.500 --> 00:21:23.470
Where am I?

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:24.720
In a cave.

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:26.010
In Puppy's cave.

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:26.890
Puppy's?

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:28.550
Yep, that's what we've named it.

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:36.120
There's no glory in a pirate saving another pirate.

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:36.850
However...

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:39.560
Well, I guess this courageous act
proves that you have a heart.

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:43.030
We've discussed it with each other...

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:46.360
If you make honourable amends,

00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:49.660
we will not report you to the authorities.

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:52.290
Really, are you serious?

00:21:59.240 --> 00:22:01.800
Am I glad to hear that.

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:03.930
In that case, what about
my share of the treasure...

00:22:03.930 --> 00:22:05.300
Have you no shame?!

00:22:10.280 --> 00:22:11.970
That Puppy!

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:15.280
"A bell on a full-moon night..."

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:17.480
"Th-The mansion of Flint."

00:22:17.480 --> 00:22:21.160
"45 degrees with a spyglass
on the Devil's Throne."

00:22:21.160 --> 00:22:25.290
"Aim the light through
the left eye of the skull."

00:22:28.600 --> 00:22:32.540
To      be        continued

00:22:33.690 --> 00:22:38.730
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:33.690 --> 00:22:38.730
Hey sea breeze

00:22:38.730 --> 00:22:44.540
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:38.730 --> 00:22:44.540
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:45.760 --> 00:22:50.750
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:45.760 --> 00:22:50.750
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:50.750 --> 00:22:56.190
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:50.750 --> 00:22:56.190
A word to my dear mother

00:22:56.190 --> 00:23:01.600
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:56.190 --> 00:23:01.600
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:01.600 --> 00:23:07.060
kaban ippai no

00:23:01.600 --> 00:23:07.060
And that my bag filled

00:23:07.060 --> 00:23:12.690
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:07.060 --> 00:23:12.690
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:12.690 --> 00:23:18.550
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:12.690 --> 00:23:18.550
Will be brought back

00:23:19.640 --> 00:23:25.140
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:19.640 --> 00:23:25.140
The sunset on my back

00:23:25.140 --> 00:23:31.030
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:25.140 --> 00:23:31.030
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:40.750
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:40.750
I blow out a whistle

00:23:45.310 --> 00:23:47.690
"A bell on a full-moon night..."

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:49.910
We still haven't solved this riddle.

00:23:50.510 --> 00:23:54.070
We're looking for the famous "Mansion of Flint",

00:23:54.070 --> 00:23:56.430
but without a clue, we're going in circles.

00:23:56.430 --> 00:23:59.360
Suddenly, Silver seems to have an idea.

00:23:59.360 --> 00:24:01.710
The key is in Flint's nickname.

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:02.920
That's the answer!

00:24:03.750 --> 00:24:05.150
Next time on Treasure Island:

00:24:05.150 --> 00:24:08.230
"Will the Dead Man's Chest
Shine on a Full-Moon?!"

00:24:08.230 --> 00:24:10.710
Only two more days
before the full-moon!

